  "result": "`slugify` now works in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes (13 of 13).\n\nIt handles `đ`/`Đ` before the diacritic stripping, because `đ` doesn't decompose. Truncation to 50 characters happens before trailing hyphens are trimmed, so a slug cut at 50 never ends with a hyphen.\n\nI added 11 `slugify` tests in `test/strings.test.js` next to the existing `capitalize` ones. They cover:\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics, including `đ`/`Đ`.\n- Runs of symbols collapsing into one hyphen, and leading/trailing hyphens being trimmed.\n- Digits being kept, and empty or symbol-only input returning `''`.\n- The 50-character cut: one where a hyphen lands at the cut, and one where the cut falls cleanly.",
